bbb-plugin-remote-desktop (2:0.3.0-5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Epoch bumped to 2. The retired standalone FPM bbb-wss-proxy
    package was versioned 1:3.0.0+<timestamp> (epoch 1), which always
    out-sorted this source's bbb-wss-proxy 0.3.0-N (epoch 0) in apt —
    so a stale FPM build in a repo would silently downgrade the
    fixed proxy. Epoch 2 makes this source's bbb-wss-proxy (and
    bbb-plugin-remote-desktop) permanently outrank any 1:3.0.0+...
    FPM build. The FPM packaging (collaborate/bbb-wss-proxy/ + its
    Makefile target) has been removed; bbb-wss-proxy is now built
    only as a second binary of this source.
  * bbb-wss-proxy nginx: accept /proxy as well as /proxy/. The
    location is a prefix match that a URI of exactly "/proxy" does
    not satisfy, so a share URL without the trailing slash fell
    through to BBB's catch-all and the WebSocket failed (code 1006).
    Added an exact-match location with an internal (non-redirect)
    rewrite to /proxy/, since a WebSocket handshake won't follow 3xx.

 -- Brent Baccala <cosine@freesoft.org>  Mon, 18 May 2026 03:34:25 +0000

bbb-plugin-remote-desktop (0.3.0-4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Documentation only (no code change; the shipped plugin JS is
    byte-identical to 0.3.0-3 apart from its commit-hash filename).
  * README: document the new optional `alt` button-config field and
    the no-`icon` single-letter-glyph fallback — the button fields
    table now lists label/keysym/icon/alt with a Required column, the
    Icons section and resolution order cover both, with examples.
  * README: add an "Applying changes" callout — /etc/bigbluebutton/
    bbb-html5.yml is read by bbb-apps-akka (clientSettingsOverride-
    FilePath), not bbb-web; editing it needs `systemctl restart
    bbb-apps-akka` (or `bbb-conf --restart`), and a browser reload or
    new meeting does not pick the change up. Reworded the post-install
    restart line so it no longer pins the mechanism to bbb-web.

 -- Brent Baccala <cosine@freesoft.org>  Mon, 18 May 2026 02:55:25 +0000

bbb-plugin-remote-desktop (0.3.0-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Custom-image action-bar button icons: the <img> rendered for a
    URL/path/data-URI icon now takes its alt text from a new optional
    `alt` field on the button config (falling back to `label`), and is
    given display:block + explicit 24x24 sizing so it can't collapse
    in the action bar. Previously the alt was hardcoded empty, which
    marked the image presentational and hid it from the accessibility
    tree (and from Playwright/a11y snapshots) even when it rendered.
  * Button config: a button with no `icon` now renders a single-letter
    glyph (first character of `label`, else `alt`, else blank) instead
    of silently defaulting to the built-in grid-2x2 icon.
  * bbb-vnc-collaborate: the default "Grid View" button config now
    carries alt: "Grid view" (no effect while it uses the built-in
    grid-2x2 icon; applies if the icon is changed to an image).

 -- Brent Baccala <cosine@freesoft.org>  Mon, 18 May 2026 00:43:38 +0000

bbb-plugin-remote-desktop (0.3.0-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * bbb-wss-proxy: fix session-token validation on BigBlueButton 3.0.
    The 0.3.0-1 proxy validated tokens against /bigbluebutton/api/enter,
    which was removed in BBB 3.0 (returns 404), so every connection was
    rejected with "Invalid BBB session token". Validation now uses
    /bigbluebutton/connection/legacyCheckAuthorization, the stateless
    3.0 equivalent (checks the token maps to a known meeting
    UserSession; no grails HTTP-session cookie required, unlike
    checkAuthorization / checkGraphqlAuthorization). The token is now
    passed in the x-original-uri header per BBB's nginx auth_request
    convention rather than as a query parameter.
  * bbb-wss-proxy: default BBB_WEB_URL is now http://localhost:8090.
    BBB 3.0 runs bbb-web on port 8090; the previous 8080 default was a
    2.x assumption and never connected on a stock 3.0 host.

 -- Brent Baccala <cosine@freesoft.org>  Sun, 17 May 2026 23:32:31 +0000

bbb-plugin-remote-desktop (0.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Source package now builds a second binary, bbb-wss-proxy: a
    WebSocket-to-VNC gateway that authenticates incoming connections
    against BBB's session-token API (/bigbluebutton/api/enter). The
    plugin automatically appends the user's session token to every
    share URL, so any user authenticated to a meeting reaches the
    VNC backend with valid credentials and no separate sign-in.
  * Action-bar buttons can now use custom PNG/SVG/JPEG/GIF/WebP
    images or data URIs as icons, in addition to the built-in
    plugin icons and BBB stock icons. URL-shaped values (containing
    "://", leading "/", "data:", or an image-file extension) are
    rendered as a 24x24 <img>.
  * README rewritten for a general (non-collaborate) audience:
    use-case framing, server-side requirements, operator-selector
    documentation, clipboard-sharing documentation, custom-icon
    examples, and an "optional bbb-wss-proxy" install section.
  * Add MIT LICENSE and DEP-5 debian/copyright.

 -- Brent Baccala <cosine@freesoft.org>  Thu, 14 May 2026 04:23:44 +0000

bbb-plugin-remote-desktop (0.2.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Skip the force-reconnect on initial content entry to layout. The
    force-reconnect was firing on every fresh page load (not only on
    post-screenshare re-entry), producing two back-to-back websocket
    opens — one from the initial VncDisplay mount, one from the key
    change to 1. That double-connect raced websockify's check-and-spawn
    and, for moderator/teacher sessions, also raced two inetd
    teacher_desktop sessions on the same X display.

 -- Brent Baccala <cosine@freesoft.org>  Wed, 22 Apr 2026 23:30:00 +0000

